  "Question": "If \\(10^{2y}=25,\\) then \\(10^{-y}\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-\\dfrac15\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac1{625}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac1{50}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac1{25}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The exponent \\(2y\\) suggests viewing the given power as a square:\n\\[\n(10^y)^2=10^{2y}=25.\n\\]\nA positive base raised to a real exponent is positive, so \\(10^y>0\\). Consequently, \\(10^y=5\\); the negative square root cannot apply. Opposite exponents give reciprocal values, so\n\\[\n10^{-y}=\\frac1{10^y}=\\frac15.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\dfrac15\\), choice E.",
